--- title Reading an error
--- about An error is read through paths, and that is how REBOL code asks
--- about which failure happened. Rebol's own suite is written in this
--- about idiom throughout, so an implementation whose errors are opaque
--- about cannot run any of it.

--- id errors/the-id-names-the-failure
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
e: try [1 / 0]
e/id
--- result
zero-divide

--- id errors/the-id-is-a-word-not-a-string
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note So it compares with a lit-word. Making it a string would let
--- note every assertion in the suite compile and none of them hold.
--- code
e: try [1 / 0]
type? e/id
--- result
#(word!)

--- id errors/the-type-names-the-category
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
e: try [1 / 0]
e/type
--- result
Math

--- id errors/the-type-is-a-word-too
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
e: try [1 / 0]
type? e/type
--- result
#(word!)

--- id errors/the-code-numbers-the-failure
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
e: try [1 / 0]
e/code
--- result
400

--- id errors/an-error-with-nothing-to-name
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note Dividing by zero is about no particular value, so the argument
--- note fields are none rather than absent.
--- code
e: try [1 / 0]
e/arg1
--- result
_

--- id errors/an-error-names-the-word-it-tripped-over
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
e: try [zzz]
e/arg1
--- result
zzz

--- id errors/the-id-of-a-word-with-no-value
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
e: try [zzz]
e/id
--- result
no-value

--- id errors/the-id-of-a-wrong-argument
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note The one the suite reaches for most.
--- code
e: try [1 + "a"]
e/id
--- result
expect-arg

--- id errors/the-fields-an-error-has
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note Fixed, and in this order, because code walks the result.
--- code
e: try [1 / 0]
mold words-of e
--- result
"[code type id arg1 arg2 arg3 near where]"

--- id errors/an-error-is-not-an-object
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note Even though it is read like one. OBJECT? says no, so code
--- note cannot use that to tell whether a path will work.
--- code
e: try [1 / 0]
object? e
--- result
#(false)

--- id errors/asking-for-a-field-an-error-has-not-got
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note Raises rather than answering none, because an error either has
--- note the field or the code asking is wrong.
--- code
e: try [1 / 0]
e/nonesuch
--- error script invalid-path

--- id errors/the-usual-idiom-in-one-line
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note This is what most of Rebol's own error assertions look like.
--- code
all [error? e: try [1 + "a"] e/id = 'expect-arg]
--- result
#(true)
